  "body": "### Summary\nAs a user, I want the launch to send each page once, so that the first screen is not slowed by duplicate or unneeded requests. Audit #1388, finding B1.\n\n### Observed\nDevice check of #1385 (#1276 issuecomment-7220925345, iPhone Duo, 3 cold launches): 1 account check, 1 home reload, **2 `/forum1f.php`**, no cancellation. The simulator run of the same day with the test account shows 1 (#1276 issuecomment-7212483398). One request per launch is unexplained.\n\n### What the code allows (read at `dev-swift` `1685bcc`)\n- The list's only automatic trigger is `.task(id: model.wantedFilter) { await model.onAppear() }` (`TopicListView.swift:129`). It runs again each time the list view appears (a root swap between the tab bar and the split root on a foldable, `RootNavigationView.swift:180-188`; a column shown again).\n- `TopicListModel.onAppear` (`TopicListModel.swift:278-291`): a second run while the first load is in flight sends nothing (`:269`); a second run **after** it sends a refresh when `favorites_auto_refresh` is on (`:288-289`). So the candidate is: the view appears twice at launch on that device and the setting is on. To confirm with the trace branch's `onAppear` / `load(page:)` lines.\n- If confirmed: a refresh on appear should be skipped when the page on screen is younger than a few seconds.\n\n### Launch budget (one account, start screen Favoris)\n| | SwiftHFR | Legacy @ `87fe0d1c` |\n|---|---|---|\n| Session check | 1 GET profile page per account, in a new probe session (`AccountsModel.swift:177`, `SessionRefreshFlow.swift:47`) | none |\n| Home page `/` | 1, whatever the start tab (`RootNavigationView.swift:42`) | 0 until Catégories is shown (`MainWindow.swift:220-225`) |\n| `/forum1f.php` | 1 expected, 2 observed | 1 (`Favorites.swift:773-778`) |\n| AQ feed (other host) | 1 after 3 s | 1 after 3 s (`MainWindow.swift:1609`) |\n\n### Scope\n1. Mac or device: name the trigger of the second `/forum1f.php` from the trace and remove it (test with a counting `ForumDataSource`: one favourites load per cold launch).\n2. Decide whether the home page stays eager at launch. It gives the Messages badge and the login state (`NavigationModel.isLoggedIn`), but the favourites page carries the count too (`PrivateMessageCountingSource.favorites`) and `isLoggedIn` falls back on the session. Operator's call; not coded without it.\n\nRefs #1388, #1276, #1375.",
